{"changes":["cmd/telemetry.go: new `eka telemetry report [--repo \u003cid\u003e] [--since \u003ct\u003e] [--until \u003ct\u003e] [--json]` subcommand. A streaming aggregator (telemetryAggregate) folds in-scope records per session with order-independent min/max and derives: sessions observed = distinct attributed sessions; read-before-first-write = attributed sessions with a constraint-read seq below their first write seq; gate failures = a cross-scope count of gate-refusal; repaired-in-session = attributed sessions with a gate-refusal on subject S followed by a later gate-pass on S, labelled an upper bound.","Attribution: sessionsObserved / readBeforeFirstWrite / repairedInSession share one rule (sessionId != \"\" and sessionSource != \"unattributed\"). The unattributed bucket (\"\") pools records from unrelated runs and is excluded from every per-session number (commit 0f77ca8 fixed repaired-in-session leaking into it — a confirmed false positive); gateFailures stays a cross-scope total.","Limits always emitted (never a bare number): unattributedSessions; sessionsWithoutCapture \"not-observable\" (a session that never emitted leaves no record — stated, not faked, per acceptance criterion 5); telemetryStart = the repository's stream start, period-independent (honours --repo, ignores --since/--until, commit 9af4ac4); readsEmitted and readBeforeFirstWriteIsFloor (read-before-write is a floor when no read was emitted); repairedInSessionIsUpperBound.","The report Long help documents that --since/--until fence per record (so a per-session read/repair pair can be split and those two numbers are per-window), and that readsEmitted is a cross-scope signal including the unattributed bucket. The telemetrySessionFiles discovery is shared with `list` (list behavior unchanged)."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Implemented M5 (`sto:compliance-telemetry`): `eka telemetry report` aggregates the append-only telemetry stream per repository and period into the four falsifiability numbers — sessions observed, read-a-constraint-before-first-write, gate failures, repaired-in-session — with a mandatory limits section, deterministic output and --json. A pure consumer of the stream defined by adr:038-telemetry-capture / spec:telemetry-capture:1; it invents no capture field.","tests":["go test ./cmd/ -run 'Telemetry|Report' -count=1 -\u003e ok; gofmt/vet/build clean; go test -timeout 1200s ./cmd/... ok (602s).","Compliant + non-compliant fixture: TestTelemetryReportAggregates asserts all four numbers (2 / 1 / 1 / 0); each assertion flips when its input is removed.","TestTelemetryReportRepair: refusal-\u003elater-pass on the same subject = 1; different subject = 0; pass-before-refusal = 0.","TestTelemetryReportRepairExcludesUnattributed: the identical refusal-\u003epass pair in the unattributed bucket yields repairedInSession 0 (gateFailures 1, unattributedSessions 1); the same pair in an attributed session yields 1 — non-vacuous on attribution, not on the pair.","TestTelemetryReportStartPeriodIndependent: with --since after the stream's earliest record, telemetryStart still equals the global min while sessionsObserved narrows; --repo scoping honoured.","TestTelemetryReportReadBeforeAndFloor: reads emitted -\u003e floor false; read removed -\u003e floor true with the human '\u003e= 0' note; TestTelemetryReportMalformed / InvalidAt flip on corruption / invalid at (a valid fixture exits 0 first).","TestTelemetryReportFilters / JSONStable / Empty / Unattributed: filters inclusive on `at`; --json byte-identical across two runs; empty scope exits 0 with telemetryStart empty; an unattributed session file increments unattributedSessions and not sessionsObserved."]}